WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.813
Microsoft isn't retiring Active Directory;
it still supports and develops it.

2
00:00:04.813 --> 00:00:08.887
But every road now points to the
cloud, and some of the dates are real.

3
00:00:08.887 --> 00:00:13.545
NTLM is deprecated, and its
first version is already

4
00:00:13.545 --> 00:00:17.987
gone from Windows 11 24H2
and Windows Server 2025.

5
00:00:17.987 --> 00:00:22.513
Entra ID now blocks sync from taking
over privileged cloud accounts.

6
00:00:22.513 --> 00:00:25.055
And the date to circle is April 7, 2027:

7
00:00:25.055 --> 00:00:29.464
by then every Connect Sync server
has to be on a current version

8
00:00:29.464 --> 00:00:34.212
with application-based authentication,
or synchronization stops.

9
00:00:34.212 --> 00:00:38.940
Behind the dates is a direction:
Cloud Sync replacing Connect Sync,

10
00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:41.949
and cloud authentication instead of AD FS.

11
00:00:41.949 --> 00:00:43.850
The trap is lift and shift.

12
00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:49.397
Sync the forest as it stands, and twenty-five
years of organizational units (OUs),

13
00:00:49.397 --> 00:00:53.750
stale accounts and undocumented
trusts arrive in the tenant.

14
00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:58.936
Meanwhile the governance that hierarchy
carried, who could manage what and where

15
00:00:58.936 --> 00:01:03.650
policy applied, gets left behind, because
Entra ID has no OU tree to carry it.
